# Component Patterns

Components are reusable UI elements following React 19 patterns.

## Component Structure

- **UI Components**: Base components in `src/components/ui/` (shadcn/ui)
- **Feature Components**: Higher-level components in `src/components/`
- **Page Components**: Page-level components in `src/pages/` (thin wrappers referenced by route files)
- Use functional components with TypeScript
- Prefer named exports over default exports

## Component Props

- Use `React.ComponentProps<'div'>` or similar for extending HTML element props
- Accept `className` prop and merge with `cn()` utility
- Use TypeScript interfaces for complex prop types

```typescript
export function Component({
  className,
  ...props
}: React.ComponentProps<'div'>) {
  return <div className={cn('base-classes', className)} {...props} />;
}
```

## shadcn/ui Components

- Use components from `@/components/ui/` (shadcn/ui New York style)
- Components are built on Radix UI primitives with Tailwind styling
- Import from `@/components/ui/` not directly from Radix

## Form Components

- Use `Field`, `FieldLabel`, `FieldDescription`, `FieldGroup` from `@/components/ui/field`
- Use `Input`, `Button`, `Select` from `@/components/ui/`
- Handle validation with Zod schemas
- Use `toast` from `sonner` for error notifications

## Styling

- Use Tailwind CSS classes
- Use `cn()` utility from `@/lib/utils` for conditional classes
- Follow shadcn/ui New York style patterns

## State Management

- Use `useState` for local component state
- Use `useContext` for accessing global context (Auth, etc.)
- Use TanStack Query for server state

